Carried patch, Windows only: MFEM opens meshes in binary mode.

general/zstr.hpp's ifgzstream opens with std::ios_base::in, text mode, so on
Windows \r\n inside a binary mesh (Gmsh "2.2 1 8") is rewritten and the solve
aborts with "vertices indices are not unique". MFEM's ofstream already adds
std::ios_base::binary; this gives the reader the same. No effect on Linux
and macOS; CRLF text meshes are unaffected, since the text readers already
filter_dos(). Still present on MFEM master.

--- a/general/zstr.hpp
+++ b/general/zstr.hpp
@@ -777,9 +777,11 @@
      public std::istream
 {
 public:
+   // Binary, like ofstream above: on Windows a text-mode stream rewrites \r\n inside
+   // binary meshes (Gmsh "2.2 1 8", VTK binary). Text readers already filter_dos().
    explicit ifgzstream(const std::string &filename)
       : zstr::detail::strict_fstream_holder<strict_fstream::ifstream>(filename,
-                                                                      std::ios_base::in),
+                                                                      std::ios_base::in | std::ios_base::binary),
         std::istream(nullptr)
    {
 #ifdef MFEM_USE_ZLIB
